// Title: Bypass UAC via CMSTP
// ID: e66779cc-383e-4224-a3a4-267eeb585c40
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: E.M. Anhaus (originally from Atomic Blue Detections, Endgame), oscd.community
// Date: 2019-10-24
// Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.stealth, attack.t1548.002, attack.t1218.003
// Description: Detect commandline usage of Microsoft Connection Manager Profile Installer (cmstp.exe) to install specially formatted local .INF files
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_/s*" or process.command_line like "*_-s*" or process.command_line like "*_/au*" or process.command_line like "*_-au*" or process.command_line like "*_/ni*" or process.command_line like "*_-ni*")) and ((process.executable endswith "\\cmstp.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "CMSTP.EXE")))
